     "answer": "The staff cost to the contract completion date was put at $300K, presented in the 10 September governance meeting commercial forecast. [1]\n\n- The forecast showed a $160K loss plus $150K supervision overrun and $300K staff cost to contract date [1]\n- It was decided to add a $300K staff cost management adjustment that month (Ben) and to report to the contract PC date on a worst-case basis with opportunity upside (Carl) [1]\n- Discussion noted the current CCC of about $425K and another $300K if four-class staffing continues — \"six hundred all round\" [2]\n- A further ~$125K staff shortfall was flagged against the target date, versus ~$125K on the spot for the contract (PC) date [3]\n\nNote: no project document on file addresses this; the figures are from meeting records only.",
     "final_raw": "The staff cost to the contract completion date was put at $300K, presented in the 10 September governance meeting commercial forecast. [R2]\n\n- The forecast showed a $160K loss plus $150K supervision overrun and $300K staff cost to contract date [R2]\n- It was decided to add a $300K staff cost management adjustment that month (Ben) and to report to the contract PC date on a worst-case basis with opportunity upside (Carl) [R2]\n- Discussion noted the current CCC of about $425K and another $300K if four-class staffing continues — \"six hundred all round\" [R1]\n- A further ~$125K staff shortfall was flagged against the target date, versus ~$125K on the spot for the contract (PC) date [R3]\n\nNote: no project document on file addresses this; the figures are from meeting records only.",
